<%# THE PHONE TAB BAR (Shop manual spec §7, slice 3): below 720px the strip's four places move here,
    exactly the four, lit by the same `sidebar_current` (through `place_aria`), so the strip and the
    bar cannot disagree. shell.css shows it below 720px only.

    THERE IS NO MORE TAB ANY LONGER. It held what the rail carried beyond four tabs; now the account
    button's menu, in the strip at every width, holds Settings, Account, Help, the theme and Sign
    out, and Trash and 3D models are rows in the Library's column. Labelled "Main" like the strip's places,
    because only one of the two is ever displayed. %>
<nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Main">
  <% strip_places.each do |place, label, path, icon| %>
    <%= link_to path, class: "tabbar-link", "aria-current": place_aria(place) do %>
      <%= rail_icon(icon) %><span><%= label %></span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</nav>
